{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MmMEGuuc71UTC6JyEkGnv1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Shareable Anchor Distro + `/onboard` — MASTER PLAN (FROZEN, Shark-converged)\n2\t\n3\t> Crucible, 2026-06-23. Branch `share-distro` off Anchor master. Shark-Tank R1 (3 sharks, 4 verified\n4\t> BLOCKERs + many MAJORs) converged into this plan. Scope: **FULL v1** (John) — cross-platform core +\n5\t> cross-platform live terminals + per-OS auto-service + vendored skills + `/onboard` + private GitHub. Every\n6\t> Shark fix is folded in as a concrete wave (see IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md).\n7\t\n8\t## North Star (LOCKED — John, 2026-06-23)\n9\tProduce a clean, shareable Anchor git repo — **zero personal data** — with the **trio (researchPrime,\n10\tCrucible, Foreman) + Gandalf** skills vendored in, that a collaborator clones and brings up on their own\n11\tmachine (**Windows / macOS / Linux**) with one **`/onboard`** command: installs the skills, scaffolds a fresh\n12\tempty Anchor, sets their **own** token, registers the background service, and starts the dashboard. Reuse\n13\t`distro.py`'s deny-by-default builder; **never ship the author's data, history, or host paths.**\n14\t\n15\t## Locked decisions (post-Shark)\n16\t1. **Clean repo via `distro.py`** (deny-by-default + no-PII/secrets scan + stdlib-import scan), EXTENDED to\n17\t   (a) treat `vendor/bundled-skills/**` as **vendored** (skip the import + high-entropy scans like `vendor/`),\n18\t   and (b) add a **build-host-path** detector (`C:\\dev\\…`, `/Users/<u>/`, `/home/<u>/`) to the PII scan\n19\t   (fixes the 157 leaking host paths the scan misses today). [BLOCKERs S1-1/2/3, S3-1/3]\n20\t2. **Skills vendored under `vendor/bundled-skills/{researchPrime,crucible,foreman,gandalf}/` via\n21\t   `git archive <commit>`** — NOT a working-tree copy. `git archive` auto-excludes `.git/`, gitignored files\n22\t   (node_modules, `*-out/`, `runs/`, `.env`, `.foreman/`, `*-checkpoint.json`, the named personal logs\n23\t   `EXECUTION-LOG.md`/`DECISION-LOG.md`/`CLAUDE_hist.md`), and dirty working state. `SOURCES.md` stamps the\n24\t   **archived commit** (honest provenance). A residual-scrub pass genericizes any remaining host paths / test\n25\t   PII before staging. [BLOCKERs S3-2/S1-4, S3-10]\n26\t3. **`/onboard` = a REPO-LOCAL Claude Code skill** (shipped in the repo so it's discoverable on clone+open,\n27\t   no prior install) that invokes the installer `onboard.py`. The README documents `python onboard.py` as the\n28\t   guaranteed-works bring-up (installs the skills, after which `/onboard` + the trio/Gandalf are available).\n29\t   [fixes the S2-4 chicken-and-egg while honoring \"`/onboard` is the entry\"]\n30\t4. **Cross-platform terminals via the existing `pty_manager` backend seam**: keep `pywinpty` on Windows; add\n31\t   a **stdlib `pty`-module POSIX backend** for macOS/Linux (the stdlib `pty`/`os` modules — NO new dependency).\n32\t   `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND` already selects the backend; auto-select by OS. [resolves OPEN#1 stdlib-only]\n33\t5. **`/onboard` registers the background service per-OS** — NSSM (Windows) · launchd user-agent (macOS) ·\n34\t   systemd-user (Linux) — through a NEW injectable **`ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD` seam** (stubbed in tests, like\n35\t   `ANCHOR_GH_CMD`), with a **foreground/`nohup` fallback** when registration isn't possible (no elevation /\n36\t   no service manager). Service env captures PATH (`claude`/`node`) + the token. [BLOCKER S1-6 made tractable]\n37\t6. **POSIX single-instance guard**: add a pidfile/`EADDRINUSE`-exit guard for non-Windows (the Windows\n38\t   `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` guard has no POSIX equivalent today → the duplicate-server bug recurs). [S1-5]\n39\t7. **Token**: `onboard.py` GENERATES a random `ANCHOR_TOKEN` per machine, written to a file **outside the\n40\t   repo tree** (or repo `.gitignore`'d AND manifest-excluded by construction); service unit files written\n41\t   `chmod 600`. Never printed to a shared log, never committed; `build_distro` stays clean after onboard runs.\n42\t   [S3-4]\n43\t8. **Skill install = COPY by default** (deterministic, no privilege), **symlink opt-in**; refuse-don't-clobber\n44\t   when a target `~/.claude/skills/<name>` already points elsewhere (protects the AUTHOR's own live dev\n45\t   symlinks). [S1-7, S3-5]\n46\t9. **Ship to a NEW PRIVATE GitHub repo** via `ANCHOR_GH_CMD` → `gh repo create --private`; gate the push on a\n47\t   **clean `build_distro` scan**; spell out the no-`gh` manual path (`git init`/`remote add`/push). [S1-8, S3-8]\n48\t10. **Windows-ism audit**: the shipped UI/comments must not hardcode `nssm`/`gwl-server`/the author's host\n49\t    (generic strings); the daily healthcheck + scheduling are honestly scoped per-OS (cron/launchd-timer or\n50\t    documented-Windows-only). [S3-7, S1-9]\n51\t\n52\t## Architecture\n53\t- **`distro.py` / `dist_manifest.txt`** — extend: classify `vendor/bundled-skills/**` as vendored; add the\n54\t  build-host-path PII detector; allow-list the vendored skills + `onboard.py` + the repo-local `/onboard`\n55\t  skill + starter templates; `build_distro` ends with a clean-scan gate before any push.\n56\t- **`vendor_skills.py` (NEW, stdlib)** — `git archive <commit>` each source skill → `vendor/bundled-skills/`,\n57\t  honoring `.gitignore`, stripping `.git/`, writing `SOURCES.md`, running the residual host-path/PII scrub.\n58\t- **Starter templates** — empty `DASHBOARD.md`/`INBOX.md`/`PROJECTS.md`/`domains/*`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`/\n59\t  `CANCELLED.md`/`WEEKLY_REVIEW.md` (headers only). Onboard scaffolds only-if-absent (never clobbers).\n60\t- **`onboard.py` (NEW, stdlib, cross-platform, idempotent, resumable, never-destructive)** — detect OS +\n61\t  prereqs (Python≥3.8, node, `claude` CLI; optional `pywinpty` Windows) → install the 4 skills (copy default)\n62\t  → scaffold starter Anchor → generate+store the token → register the service via `ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD`\n63\t  (foreground fallback) → health-check `:8777` + print the URL. Honest per-OS skip messaging; rollback on a\n64\t  half-failed service step.\n65\t- **`pty_manager.py`** — add the stdlib POSIX `pty` backend; OS-auto-select.\n66\t- **`/onboard` repo-local skill** — `SKILL.md` that runs `python onboard.py`.\n67\t- **Service seam** — `ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD` (stub in tests) + per-OS registrars + the foreground fallback.\n68\t- **Tests / healthcheck** — `check_onboard_surface` (FULLY hermetic): temp `HOME`/skills-dir, stubbed\n69\t  `ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD`, stubbed `gh` (`tests/stub_gh.py` + local bare remote), `port=0`, never `:8777` / real\n70\t  home / real service / network; restores all env.\n71\t\n72\t## Risks (post-Shark, with mitigations)\n73\t- **R1 PII/host-path leak in vendored skills** → `git archive` + the new host-path detector + residual scrub +\n74\t  a clean-scan GATE on the build (Wave done-when: `build_distro` clean over the staged tree).\n75\t- **R2 per-OS service correctness/elevation** → the `ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD` seam + foreground fallback +\n76\t  stubbed-hermetic tests; the fallback alone satisfies \"bring it up,\" so a failed registrar never blocks.\n77\t- **R3 onboard destroys the author's/collaborator's setup** → copy-default + refuse-don't-clobber + resumable\n78\t  + rollback; never overwrite existing data/skills.\n79\t- **R4 POSIX duplicate-server** → the pidfile/EADDRINUSE guard (Wave 1).\n80\t- **R5 token leak** → out-of-tree/`.gitignore`'d token + `chmod 600` units + a test that build stays clean\n81\t  after onboard.\n82\t- **R6 cross-platform terminals** → stdlib `pty` POSIX backend (no new dep); Windows unchanged.\n83\t- **R7 vendoring drift** → `SOURCES.md` archived-commit stamp; re-vendor is a clean `git archive`.\n84\t\n85\t## Out of scope (v1)\n86\tAuto-syncing vendored skills with upstream; a GUI installer; multi-user/hosted Anchor; migrating an existing\n87\tuser's data (the share repo is for FRESH installs); alternate-engine (Gemini/OpenAI) keys (`.env.example`\n88\texcluded or documented-optional).\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a086159-4fbe-4523-b813-fd8819627385","uuid":"ed419b4e-176b-4a2c-bf66-4cc22182e531","timestamp":"2026-06-23T21:17:54.882Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\share-distro-v1\\MASTER-PLAN.md","content":"# Shareable Anchor Distro + `/onboard` — MASTER PLAN (FROZEN, Shark-converged)\n\n> Crucible, 2026-06-23. Branch `share-distro` off Anchor master. Shark-Tank R1 (3 sharks, 4 verified\n> BLOCKERs + many MAJORs) converged into this plan. Scope: **FULL v1** (John) — cross-platform core +\n> cross-platform live terminals + per-OS auto-service + vendored skills + `/onboard` + private GitHub. Every\n> Shark fix is folded in as a concrete wave (see IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md).\n\n## North Star (LOCKED — John, 2026-06-23)\nProduce a clean, shareable Anchor git repo — **zero personal data** — with the **trio (researchPrime,\nCrucible, Foreman) + Gandalf** skills vendored in, that a collaborator clones and brings up on their own\nmachine (**Windows / macOS / Linux**) with one **`/onboard`** command: installs the skills, scaffolds a fresh\nempty Anchor, sets their **own** token, registers the background service, and starts the dashboard. Reuse\n`distro.py`'s deny-by-default builder; **never ship the author's data, history, or host paths.**\n\n## Locked decisions (post-Shark)\n1. **Clean repo via `distro.py`** (deny-by-default + no-PII/secrets scan + stdlib-import scan), EXTENDED to\n   (a) treat `vendor/bundled-skills/**` as **vendored** (skip the import + high-entropy scans like `vendor/`),\n   and (b) add a **build-host-path** detector (`C:\\dev\\…`, `/Users/<u>/`, `/home/<u>/`) to the PII scan\n   (fixes the 157 leaking host paths the scan misses today). [BLOCKERs S1-1/2/3, S3-1/3]\n2. **Skills vendored under `vendor/bundled-skills/{researchPrime,crucible,foreman,gandalf}/` via\n   `git archive <commit>`** — NOT a working-tree copy. `git archive` auto-excludes `.git/`, gitignored files\n   (node_modules, `*-out/`, `runs/`, `.env`, `.foreman/`, `*-checkpoint.json`, the named personal logs\n   `EXECUTION-LOG.md`/`DECISION-LOG.md`/`CLAUDE_hist.md`), and dirty working state. `SOURCES.md` stamps the\n   **archived commit** (honest provenance). A residual-scrub pass genericizes any remaining host paths / test\n   PII before staging. [BLOCKERs S3-2/S1-4, S3-10]\n3. **`/onboard` = a REPO-LOCAL Claude Code skill** (shipped in the repo so it's discoverable on clone+open,\n   no prior install) that invokes the installer `onboard.py`. The README documents `python onboard.py` as the\n   guaranteed-works bring-up (installs the skills, after which `/onboard` + the trio/Gandalf are available).\n   [fixes the S2-4 chicken-and-egg while honoring \"`/onboard` is the entry\"]\n4. **Cross-platform terminals via the existing `pty_manager` backend seam**: keep `pywinpty` on Windows; add\n   a **stdlib `pty`-module POSIX backend** for macOS/Linux (the stdlib `pty`/`os` modules — NO new dependency).\n   `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND` already selects the backend; auto-select by OS. [resolves OPEN#1 stdlib-only]\n5. **`/onboard` registers the background service per-OS** — NSSM (Windows) · launchd user-agent (macOS) ·\n   systemd-user (Linux) — through a NEW injectable **`ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD` seam** (stubbed in tests, like\n   `ANCHOR_GH_CMD`), with a **foreground/`nohup` fallback** when registration isn't possible (no elevation /\n   no service manager). Service env captures PATH (`claude`/`node`) + the token. [BLOCKER S1-6 made tractable]\n6. **POSIX single-instance guard**: add a pidfile/`EADDRINUSE`-exit guard for non-Windows (the Windows\n   `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` guard has no POSIX equivalent today → the duplicate-server bug recurs). [S1-5]\n7. **Token**: `onboard.py` GENERATES a random `ANCHOR_TOKEN` per machine, written to a file **outside the\n   repo tree** (or repo `.gitignore`'d AND manifest-excluded by construction); service unit files written\n   `chmod 600`. Never printed to a shared log, never committed; `build_distro` stays clean after onboard runs.\n   [S3-4]\n8. **Skill install = COPY by default** (deterministic, no privilege), **symlink opt-in**; refuse-don't-clobber\n   when a target `~/.claude/skills/<name>` already points elsewhere (protects the AUTHOR's own live dev\n   symlinks). [S1-7, S3-5]\n9. **Ship to a NEW PRIVATE GitHub repo** via `ANCHOR_GH_CMD` → `gh repo create --private`; gate the push on a\n   **clean `build_distro` scan**; spell out the no-`gh` manual path (`git init`/`remote add`/push). [S1-8, S3-8]\n10. **Windows-ism audit**: the shipped UI/comments must not hardcode `nssm`/`gwl-server`/the author's host\n    (generic strings); the daily healthcheck + scheduling are honestly scoped per-OS (cron/launchd-timer or\n    documented-Windows-only). [S3-7, S1-9]\n\n## Architecture\n- **`distro.py` / `dist_manifest.txt`** — extend: classify `vendor/bundled-skills/**` as vendored; add the\n  build-host-path PII detector; allow-list the vendored skills + `onboard.py` + the repo-local `/onboard`\n  skill + starter templates; `build_distro` ends with a clean-scan gate before any push.\n- **`vendor_skills.py` (NEW, stdlib)** — `git archive <commit>` each source skill → `vendor/bundled-skills/`,\n  honoring `.gitignore`, stripping `.git/`, writing `SOURCES.md`, running the residual host-path/PII scrub.\n- **Starter templates** — empty `DASHBOARD.md`/`INBOX.md`/`PROJECTS.md`/`domains/*`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`/\n  `CANCELLED.md`/`WEEKLY_REVIEW.md` (headers only). Onboard scaffolds only-if-absent (never clobbers).\n- **`onboard.py` (NEW, stdlib, cross-platform, idempotent, resumable, never-destructive)** — detect OS +\n  prereqs (Python≥3.8, node, `claude` CLI; optional `pywinpty` Windows) → install the 4 skills (copy default)\n  → scaffold starter Anchor → generate+store the token → register the service via `ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD`\n  (foreground fallback) → health-check `:8777` + print the URL. Honest per-OS skip messaging; rollback on a\n  half-failed service step.\n- **`pty_manager.py`** — add the stdlib POSIX `pty` backend; OS-auto-select.\n- **`/onboard` repo-local skill** — `SKILL.md` that runs `python onboard.py`.\n- **Service seam** — `ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD` (stub in tests) + per-OS registrars + the foreground fallback.\n- **Tests / healthcheck** — `check_onboard_surface` (FULLY hermetic): temp `HOME`/skills-dir, stubbed\n  `ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD`, stubbed `gh` (`tests/stub_gh.py` + local bare remote), `port=0`, never `:8777` / real\n  home / real service / network; restores all env.\n\n## Risks (post-Shark, with mitigations)\n- **R1 PII/host-path leak in vendored skills** → `git archive` + the new host-path detector + residual scrub +\n  a clean-scan GATE on the build (Wave done-when: `build_distro` clean over the staged tree).\n- **R2 per-OS service correctness/elevation** → the `ANCHOR_SERVICE_CMD` seam + foreground fallback +\n  stubbed-hermetic tests; the fallback alone satisfies \"bring it up,\" so a failed registrar never blocks.\n- **R3 onboard destroys the author's/collaborator's setup** → copy-default + refuse-don't-clobber + resumable\n  + rollback; never overwrite existing data/skills.\n- **R4 POSIX duplicate-server** → the pidfile/EADDRINUSE guard (Wave 1).\n- **R5 token leak** → out-of-tree/`.gitignore`'d token + `chmod 600` units + a test that build stays clean\n  after onboard.\n- **R6 cross-platform terminals** → stdlib `pty` POSIX backend (no new dep); Windows unchanged.\n- **R7 vendoring drift** → `SOURCES.md` archived-commit stamp; re-vendor is a clean `git archive`.\n\n## Out of scope (v1)\nAuto-syncing vendored skills with upstream; a GUI installer; multi-user/hosted Anchor; migrating an existing\nuser's data (the share repo is for FRESH installs); alternate-engine (Gemini/OpenAI) keys (`.env.example`\nexcluded or documented-optional).\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
